{
  "source": "FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_P05\nVAR_INPUT\n    Gap_Exceeded : BOOL;\n    Weld_E_Stop_NC : BOOL;\n    DebounceTime : TIME;\nEND_VAR\nVAR_OUTPUT\n    Operator_Alert : BOOL;\n    Weld_Soft_Start_Active : BOOL;\nEND_VAR\nVAR\n    InitTimer : TON;\n    DebounceTimer : TON;\n    MinHoldTimer : TON;\n    SafeDebounceTime : TIME;\n    EStopActive : BOOL;\nEND_VAR\n\n(*\n  Conflict report:\n  K3 asks for immediate Operator_Alert reset when Gap_Exceeded becomes FALSE.\n  C9 asks that Operator_Alert, once set, remain TRUE for at least 500 ms.\n  These cannot both hold if Gap_Exceeded falls within 500 ms after alarm set.\n  The logic below enforces the 500 ms minimum alarm pulse during non-emergency\n  operation. Emergency stop (K4/C1) still overrides and clears the alarm immediately.\n*)\n\n(* 5 s power-up inhibition. Weld_Soft_Start_Active represents only this period. *)\nInitTimer(IN := TRUE, PT := T#5s);\nWeld_Soft_Start_Active := NOT InitTimer.Q;\n\n(* Emergency stop is active when Weld_E_Stop_NC is FALSE. *)\nEStopActive := NOT Weld_E_Stop_NC;\n\n(* Boundary handling: DebounceTime must be positive. Non-positive values are\n   clamped to one scan cycle to avoid undefined TON behavior. *)\nSafeDebounceTime := DebounceTime;\nIF SafeDebounceTime <= T#0s THEN\n    SafeDebounceTime := T#20ms;\nEND_IF;\n\n(* During emergency stop or initialization inhibition, alarm must be FALSE. *)\nIF EStopActive OR NOT InitTimer.Q THEN\n    Operator_Alert := FALSE;\nEND_IF;\n\n(* Debounce accumulation only during normal monitoring, no emergency stop,\n   and while Gap_Exceeded is TRUE. *)\nDebounceTimer(\n    IN := (NOT EStopActive) AND InitTimer.Q AND Gap_Exceeded,\n    PT := SafeDebounceTime\n);\n\n(* Alarm set only after debounce time has elapsed during normal monitoring. *)\nIF (NOT EStopActive) AND InitTimer.Q AND Gap_Exceeded AND DebounceTimer.Q THEN\n    Operator_Alert := TRUE;\nEND_IF;\n\n(* Minimum alarm pulse timer: 500 ms after alarm set. Reset by emergency stop. *)\nMinHoldTimer(\n    IN := Operator_Alert AND (NOT EStopActive),\n    PT := T#500ms\n);\n\n(* Alarm reset after gap clears and minimum pulse has elapsed. Emergency stop\n   and initialization inhibition are handled above with higher priority. *)\nIF (NOT EStopActive) AND InitTimer.Q AND (NOT Gap_Exceeded) AND MinHoldTimer.Q THEN\n    Operator_Alert := FALSE;\nEND_IF;\n\nEND_FUNCTION_BLOCK\n",
